{"name":"Brass Trumpet","hex":"#d3b280","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metallic alloy of copper and zinc used in many industrial and plumbing applications.","A memorial or sepulchral tablet usually made of brass or latten: a monumental brass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of brass, of or pertaining to brass.","Of the color of brass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brass"},{"term":"trumpet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical instrument of the brass family, generally tuned to the key of B-flat; by extension, any type of lip-vibrated aerophone, most often valveless and not chromatic.","Someone who plays the trumpet; a trumpeter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sound loudly, be amplified","To play the trumpet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trumpet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brass","blocks":[{"text":"Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc, in proportions which can be varied to achieve different colours and mechanical, electrical, acoustic, and chemical properties, but copper typically has the larger proportion, generally 2⁄3 copper and 1⁄3 zinc. In use since prehistoric times, it is a substitutional alloy: atoms of the two constituents may replace each other within the same crystal structure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg/330px-Planispheric_Astrolabe_MET_DP105325.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brass","wikidata":"Q39782"},{"title":"Trumpet","blocks":[{"text":"The trumpet is a brass instrument. The most common type of trumpet is a transposing instrument in B♭, with pitches sounding a whole step lower than written. The trumpet family includes instruments ranging from the piccolo trumpet, with the highest register in the brass family, to the bass trumpet, pitched one octave below the standard B♭ or C trumpet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg/330px-Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpet","wikidata":"Q8338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg/500px-Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg/500px-Brass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_%28Netherlands%29%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brass lectern with an eagle, attributed to Aert van Tricht, Limburg (Netherlands), circa 1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrass_lectern_in_the_form_of_an_eagle_attributed_to_Aert_van_Tricht_the_Elder%2C_Limburg_(Netherlands)%2C_c._1500%2C_The_Cloisters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg/500px-Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg/1280px-Microstructure_of_rolled_and_annealed_brass%3B_magnification_400X.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par